/*
 * Teaching layer — the surface that makes 0→80 possible.
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
 * The scored bank is a measurement instrument. Its questions are generated by
 * recombining four harvested sentences per concept, so a learner arriving cold
 * meets a graded item before anything has explained the idea or the words it is
 * written in. Measured before this file existed: a case question's own primer
 * introduced 19% of the vocabulary that case used, and 10 of 64 cases had a
 * primer that introduced none of it.
 *
 * WHAT A LESSON IS
 * One lecture, taught once, before anything about that lecture is scored:
 *   objective  — what you will be able to do, in plain words
 *   explainer  — the idea itself, ~150-220 words, no jargon that is not glossed
 *   worked     — one concrete case with real numbers, run end to end
 *   glossary   — every term the lecture introduces, defined at point of use
 *   connects   — the handoff to the next lecture, so the module reads as a path
 *
 * AUTHORING CONTRACT
 * Prose here is authored, not extracted. `tools/build_t6_lessons.mjs` produces
 * candidates from the Term 6 pack (objectives, glossary terms with first_seen,
 * worked-example lines) into work/t6_lessons/, and this file is written against
 * that output. Extraction alone cannot ship: the dense files are transcript
 * bullets and some are incoherent out of context. This mirrors the split that
 * app/sets/t6_diagnoses.js already uses for hand-authored diagnoses.
 *
 * Every `glossary` term must be one the course actually uses at or before this
 * lecture. tools/validate_t6_bank.js enforces that against the lossless
 * transcripts — not the concept index, which is a retrieval candidate list —
 * and fails the build when a scheduled question uses a term no lesson
 * introduced. That gate is what keeps 0→80 true for lectures authored later.
 *
 * BEFORE AUTHORING HERE, read docs/authoring/LESSON-AUTHORING-PROTOCOL.md. It
 * carries the batch procedure, the gates in order, and the four traps that have
 * already cost a session (LAW-47 through LAW-50). `node tools/check_lesson_file.mjs
 * "<pack>"` prints the exact next batch of lectures to write.
 *
 * STATUS: BRGSA complete — 50 lectures, 8 modules. IBM, SCLM, and SPMS
 * outstanding (233 lectures). All content here is new and carries
 * WAITING_OWNER_CONTENT_ACCEPTANCE.
 */
